How it sets up the stand-in fleet: a snapshot folder with restore.sh in the test's RELEASES folder (so undo has something to go back to); the scripted stand-in model (model-script.json) calls stop_model on the first turn and undo_update on the carry-on turn; the request is sent through Funnel with the session cookie, so the turn's viewer has `session`.

Why it fails without the change: the carry-on viewer has no session, ownerHere is true, undoUpdate() runs (in the stand-in fleet it only writes the audit and a notice), so the undo_update audit line has outcome 'started' and a 'rollback' line exists. With the change the line's outcome is 'question' and there is no 'rollback' line. The positive wait for the undo_update line is on purpose: an assertion of only "no outcome other than question" could pass falsely if the call had errored.

