- Every `writePrivate` save (all 24 callers) is synced before the rename, and a failed save removes its temporary file and still throws the same error.
- Only a file that `readKept` has read in this process gets `<file>.prev`: added-models.json, found-setups.json, verified.json, validations.json, saved-workflows.json, desired.json, memory.json. Every writer of those reads through `readKept` first, so no call site changes. main.json is read with `readKept` but written by `writeMainFile`, so it gets no `.prev` and takes the "starts empty" wording.
- A failed `.prev` copy never fails the save.
- The fall-back happens only when the file exists, is not JSON, and the set-aside rename worked. A missing file (ENOENT) stays empty. A read error stays the 503 "try again".

