// Docker's own log of every container Spark Console creates is capped at three 50 MB files (150 MB). Without this it
// never rotates, and it sits under /var/lib/docker where the console (no sudo) can't trim it: the brain's grows for
// months. The driver is named so the cap is valid whatever a Spark's Docker default is (a default like journald
// refuses max-size and the start fails). `docker logs` reads it as before. It is set when a container is created, so
// one made earlier keeps its old log until its next start (the brain: its next start from the page, not a restart).
