Then, in order:

1. In the part that holds change_console's job, add at top level:

/* a self-change that stopped at its limit (H9) */
const STUCK_FILE = `${STATE_DIR}/self-change-stuck.json`;
const STUCK_TEST = /^[a-z0-9-]{1,60}\.test\.mjs$/;
// Names only test files the installed source already has; a file the engine wrote is counted, never named
// (the line goes into Sparkie's notes and to Telegram).
function markStuck({ why, runs, failing = [], known }) {
  const names = [...new Set(failing.map(f => String(f).split('/').pop()))];
  const named = names.filter(f => STUCK_TEST.test(f) && known.has(f)).sort().slice(0, 20);
  writePrivate(STUCK_FILE, { at: new Date().toISOString(), build: BUILD, why: why === 'time' ? 'time' : 'tests', runs, failing: named, others: names.length - named.length });
}
const clearStuck = () => { try { unlinkSync(STUCK_FILE); } catch {} };
// The record while it stands: this build's, well-formed. Anything else is no record (never a throw).
function selfChangeStuck() {
  const s = readJson(STUCK_FILE);
  if (!s || typeof s !== 'object' || s.build !== BUILD || typeof s.at !== 'string' || Number.isNaN(Date.parse(s.at))) return null;
  const n = (v, max) => Math.max(0, Math.min(max, Math.trunc(Number(v)) || 0));
  return { at: new Date(s.at).toISOString(), why: s.why === 'time' ? 'time' : 'tests', runs: n(s.runs, 9),
    failing: (Array.isArray(s.failing) ? s.failing : []).filter(f => typeof f === 'string' && STUCK_TEST.test(f)).slice(0, 20), others: n(s.others, 999) };
}
function stuckLine() {
  const s = selfChangeStuck();
  if (!s) return null;
  const named = s.failing.slice(0, 3), total = s.failing.length + s.others, rest = total - named.length;
  const still = total ? ` ${total} test file${total === 1 ? ' still fails' : 's still fail'}${named.length ? `: ${named.join(', ')}${rest ? ` and ${rest} more` : ''}` : ''}.` : '';
  const why = s.why === 'time' ? 'it ran out of time' : `its tests still failed after ${s.runs} full run${s.runs === 1 ? '' : 's'}`;
  return `Sparkie couldn’t finish the change to its own code asked for on ${s.at.slice(0, 10)}: ${why}.${still} Nothing was installed. To try again, ask Sparkie in Spark Console. If the fault came with the last update, go back a build ${consoleSparkWords()}: bash ~/.local/share/spark-console/go-back.sh. If Spark Console won’t open: ~/.local/share/spark-console/RECOVERY.txt.`;
}

(readJson, writePrivate, unlinkSync, BUILD, STATE_DIR and consoleSparkWords all exist today: 03-identity.mjs, 01-setup.mjs, 20-words.mjs. Keep the curly apostrophes.)

2. In the change_console job:
 - Once the job exists (after its refusals and claims): clearStuck();
 - On the one path where the job ends because its budget is used up (the full-test-run count, why 'tests'; or the minutes, why 'time'), before the job is ended as failed: markStuck({ why, runs: <full test runs done>, failing: <test files that failed in the last full run, from the result the job already reads; [] if none finished>, known: <new Set(readdirSync(`${SRC}/test`)) taken when the job copied the installed source, before the engine ran> }).
 - Never call markStuck on any other ending: cancelled, paused, refused, the engine or container could not start, a Spark off, a console restart, or anything after the tests passed (waiting for the owner's yes is not budget). That keeps "Nothing was installed" true by construction.

3. 16-actions.mjs, sparkieCheck: in the branch step 39 adds for change_console, AND !selfChangeStuck() into `clear`. While the record stands, Sparkie's own call (a carry-on turn included) comes back through the existing propose() as a button. The owner's press, or the owner's own POST /actions, starts the job, which clears the record. No new argument, schema field or question text.

4. H4's list builder: add stuckLine() as the FIRST source, in the shape the other sources use, so the 8-line cap never drops it. Where a source carries a key for H5's send-once, use `self-change-stuck:${selfChangeStuck().at}`. Nothing else: /status, Sparkie's notes, fleet_status, "Anything need me?" and the one Telegram line all come from that list.

